===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|difficulty}} A [[difficulty]] that has to be resolved or dealt with.
#: {{syn|en|rub}}
#: {{hyper|en|challenge#Noun|issue#Noun|obstacle#Noun}}
#: {{ux|en|She's leaving because she faced numerous '''problems''' to do with racism.}}
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I|text=“{{...}} it is not fair of you to bring against mankind double weapons&thinsp;! Dangerous enough you are as woman alone, without bringing to your aid those gifts of mind suited to '''problems''' which men have been accustomed to arrogate to themselves.”}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=February 3 1999|author={{w|Anthony Horowitz}}; et al|chapter=Strangler's Wood|title={{w|Midsomer Murders}}
|passage=Kate's very good with '''problems''', Chief Inspector. Other people's, anyway.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2014-03-07| author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/nicole-vulser Nicole Vulser]| volume=190| issue=13| page=30 |magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| title=Perfume manufacturers must cope with the scarcity of precious supplies|url=http://www.theguardian.com/business/2014/mar/04/chanel-perfume-legislation-guerlain-loreal| passage=The perfume industry is facing a major '''problem''': maintaining constant levels of quality is crucial, but it is increasingly difficult to obtain a regular supply of all the necessary natural ingredients.}}
## An [[addiction]], other substance use disorder, or comparable psychological challenge.
##: {{hypo|en|drinking problem|drug problem}}
##: {{ux|en|I think he has a gambling '''problem'''. Lending him money will probably only make it worse.}}
##: {{ux|en|I think he has a nose candy '''problem'''. Lending him money will probably only make it worse.}}
# {{senseid|en|schoolwork exercise}} A [[question]] to be answered, [[schoolwork]] [[exercise]].
#: {{ux|en|Study hard, but don't overdo it. The '''problems''' in the exam won't be difficult to solve.}}
# {{senseid|en|puzzling circumstance}} A [[puzzle|puzzling]] [[circumstance]].
# Objection.
#: {{ux|en|You got a '''problem''' with that?}}
# Difficulty in accepting or understanding or refusal to accept or understand.
#: {{ux|en|You made your best honest effort; if they judge you harshly, that’s their '''problem''', not yours.}}
# {{lb|en|climbing}} A set of moves required to complete a [[climb#Noun|climb]].

====Usage notes====
* Colloquially, "problem" in sense 1 can be put after an objective personal pronoun to create a noun phrase meaning "that person's/those people's problem."
: {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=Joel S. Weissman; Arnold M. Epstein|title=Falling Through the Safety Net: Insurance Status and Access to Health Care|page=30|text=Until Middle America understands lack of insurance and underinsurance as '''an "us" problem''' rather than '''a "them" problem''', the motivation for change will be diminished.}}

